[# Conformance gate policy (toggle manifest).

   DEFAULT = enforced (deny-by-default, mirroring spec/core/security.md's grant
   model): a failing fixture BLOCKS its gate. A suite/module marked `advisory`
   is the spec-first frontier — its failures are RUN and REPORTED but do NOT
   block the gate. Promote `advisory -> enforced` as the implementation lands;
   that promotion is the gate-progression control.

   Resolution order for a fixture's effective gate (most specific wins):
     per-case `gate=` attr  >  per-module entry here  >  per-suite default  >  enforced

   This manifest is module/suite-level. Per-case overrides live on the [case]
   itself (gate=advisory|pending|skip). See conformance/stdlib/AUTHORING.md and
   conformance/stdlib/SPEC-FINDINGS.md. #]

[gate-policy default=enforced

  [# core program + format suites: fully enforced (no frontier carve-out — the
     code.txt frontier is driven to zero by the spec-compliance effort). #]
  [suite name=code default=enforced]

  [# stdlib: implemented modules are enforced; not-yet-implemented modules are
     advisory (their fixtures are the spec-first worklist — red until built,
     must not block). Flip a module to enforced the moment it lands. #]
  [suite name=stdlib default=enforced
    [# implemented + enforced: bytes env format hash path random strings time uuid
       (left at the suite default; listed here for the reader) #]
    [module name=bytes   gate=enforced]
    [module name=env     gate=enforced reason='ENFORCED, all cases green; env-038 unblocked — operator-elements now propagate err-value operands uniformly with calls (§9.2), so [= [$env:vars] [$env:vars]] surfaces CXER0271 instead of comparing the two errs (SPEC-FINDINGS AK)']
    [module name=format  gate=enforced]
    [module name=hash    gate=enforced]
    [module name=path    gate=enforced]
    [module name=random  gate=enforced]
    [module name=strings gate=enforced]
    [module name=time    gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green); §3.10 recurrence amendment landed — RFC 5545 RRULE (parse/format, BYDAY ordinals, BYSETPOS, all BY* filter/expand per §3.3.10) + 5/6-field cron + @macros, DST-aware wall-clock-local expansion, max-occurrences budget (CXER3325) and CXER3320-3326 band wired, all pure (no clock); occurrences cross-validated against a hand-rolled RFC 5545 reference for last-weekday-of-month / DST-spanning weekly / biweekly MO,WE,FR (time-117..147)']
    [module name=uuid    gate=enforced]

    [# not yet implemented -> advisory (spec-first frontier) #]
    [module name=crypto   gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green); crypto-015/028 fixtures corrected to the spec [?fallback PRIMARY [recover-with SECONDARY]] form (§10.2.4; the 2-arg shorthand is not grammar, SPEC-FINDINGS AD); 18 capability-denial cases enforced (random cap-guard on the 4 entropy generators, SPEC-FINDINGS M/N); §3.8/§3.10 JWT amendment landed — rsa-verify (RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5) + ecdsa-verify (P-256 JOSE raw r‖s) over math.big + fail-closed jwt-verify/jwks-parse/claim/jwk-by-kid, cross-validated against OpenSSL vectors (crypto-062..088); jwks-fetch net-gated (live transport pending like net/http, denial case enforced)']
    [module name=csv      gate=enforced reason='RFC-4180 impl complete (ENFORCED, all cases green); csv-032 asserts CRLF emission via strings:contains; csv-013 unblocked by the iterate() array-atomization core fix ($nth/$arr[N] now expand __cx_arr__ transparently per code.md §6.6, SPEC-FINDINGS AF); csv-007 comma quote-convention re-derived via real render_value']
    [module name=email    gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete + spec-faithful (61/61 ENFORCED); all 21 quote-convention expected-outputs re-derived via the real render_value (SPEC-FINDINGS Q); all 9 CXER1300-1306 error cases pass']
    [module name=ft       gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green): Porter2 stemmer, TF-IDF/BM25, boolean/phrase/field queries, snippets. Fixed 9 two-resolver [?lib a b]→two [?lib] (grammar [149]) + ft-026 put→put-doc; ft-001 spec contradiction resolved (ft.md §143 prose → map form, matching [returns map]); ft-029 unblocked by the [?directive]-balancing parser fix (SPEC-FINDINGS U/AB)']
    [module name=geo      gate=enforced reason='full impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green); coordinate model corrected — point() WRAPS cyclic longitude (200→-160) and REJECTS non-cyclic out-of-range latitude with CXER3601 (no implicit clamp); geo-004 repurposed to the wrap assertion, geo-043/044 unblocked (normalize is identity over canonical points), SPEC-FINDINGS AG; geo-052/053 WKT quote-convention re-derived via real render_value']
    [module name=html     gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green); html-001 rewritten bind-first + simple-accessor /a@href (terminal-attr unwrap), html-005/006 use [$count] not [?fn:count] (SPEC-FINDINGS AD); 17 quote-convention expected-outputs re-derived via real render_value']
    [module name=http     gate=enforced reason='L7 HTTP/1.1 client+server on net (ENFORCED, all 64 cases green): PURE introspection (status/ok/header/headers/headers-named/has-body/body-bytes/body-bytes-wire/body-text) over homoiconic [request]/[response] literals — header value renders quoted when numeric-looking (value=\'1\') else bareword (value=c), `headers` is a node-sequence, absent header is () the absence channel, present-empty header /@value is \'\' vs absent (), body-bytes is a quoted string scalar; every network verb (get/post/put/del/patch/head/options/request/send, serve/listen/accept-iter/exchange-request/respond/stop) gated on `net` via cap_guard (CXER0271 deny-lane) with the granted lane asserting the deterministic synthetic shapes ([response status=200]/[http-server]/[request]/null); pure arg/scheme validation surfaces CXER4525 (non-http(s)/relative url=, bad bind URL), CXER4539 (status-on-request, url/path misuse, CONNECT, bad method), CXER4541 (respond status ∉ 100-599), CXER4532 (body-text unsupported charset) ahead of the cap check. ONE spec contradiction logged: §3.1 bad base-url at `client` → CXER4525 is not surfaced (impl reads opts off attrs, not the {} map), so it is fixtured at `send` instead (SPEC-FINDINGS). Live round-trips (real status/headers/body, TLS, redirects, gzip/zstd decompression) are gate=pending for a network-granted harness. §3.6 SSE/streaming landed (http-065..078): server sse/send-event/heartbeat/stream-open + client sse-connect/sse-events/source-open/last-event-id share one pure [event] framing codec (symmetry invariant in vcx/tests/http_sse_test.v); pure accessors + event validation (CXER4539 empty / CXER4531 CR-LF) + net-denial (CXER0271) + synthetic wire decode round-trip enforced; live held-open transport pending']
    [module name=i18n     gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete; 44/44 green under render_value (catalogs, locale-fallback, full ICU MessageFormat, CLDR cardinal en/ru/pl/ar + ordinal en, all 5 error codes incl. CXER0271 denial) — messages returned as TextNode so rendered text emits verbatim (SPEC-FINDINGS S)']
    [module name=io       gate=enforced reason='full cap-gated §3 impl (ENFORCED, all 51 cases green); cap_guard read/write per §7 at every effect point, real os.* behind the guard; io-005/008 fixtures fixed (added [?lib cx-stdlib/bytes] + [$bytes:from-string-utf8]; the missing import/typo errored at arg-eval before the io effect point — SPEC-FINDINGS W/AJ)']
    [module name=json     gate=enforced reason='impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green); json-031/037 rewritten to assert via spec primitives [$strings:length]/[$count] (the prior [?]@length was an UNSPEC invented attribute — SPEC-FINDINGS AD); json-005 bare-string + json-030 ensure-ascii expected-outputs re-derived via real render_value']
    [module name=locale   gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green); all 28 error cases pass; locale-018/019 now assert the numeric value via tol= (f64 renders scientific 1.23e+06 — the value is exact, SPEC-FINDINGS T/AD); 14 quote-convention expected-outputs re-derived via real render_value']
    [module name=log      gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete (27/27 ENFORCED): leveled emit, structured fields, configure/min-level/sink/format, is-enabled, [$log:current-scope] over [?with-scope] dyn_context; log-012/013 were quote-convention only (map values render bare), re-derived via real render_value (SPEC-FINDINGS V)']
    [module name=math     gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete + spec-faithful (110/110 ENFORCED): trig/hyperbolic, banker rounding, statistics, 64-bit bit-ops, Miller-Rabin/gcd/lcm/factorial, IEEE-754 predicates/constants, two-complement wrapping; checked int64 +/-/* now fold in i64 with CXER3000 overflow per §4.1 (SPEC-FINDINGS AL/AM)']
    [module name=mime     gate=enforced reason='full impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green); mime-043 rewritten to bind [$first …] then /@q (parse-accept returns a [sequence element]; CXPath navigates element trees not sequence members — SPEC-FINDINGS AD); 21 double-quote-convention expected-outputs re-derived via real render_value']
    [module name=net      gate=enforced reason='full §3 cap-gated impl (ENFORCED, all 57 cases green): parse-addr/addr-to-string PURE (restricted-transport-URL grammar, IPv6 brackets/zone, unix paths, round-trip), every socket/resolver effect point gated on net via cap_guard at dispatch (CXER0271 deny-lane), close/is-open/local-addr/remote-addr capability-free. TWO spec contradictions resolved: (1) net owns CXER4500-4524, NOT the rev-7 draft 4400-band which collided with cx-stdlib/fp CXER4400-4409 (governance §9.6); (2) addr->string renamed addr-to-string — > is not a grammar NameChar (grammar.ebnf [6a]). Connection/TLS/DTLS live paths (handshake, SSRF, accept-iter) are gate=pending for a capability-granted harness']
    [module name=process  gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete (27/27 ENFORCED): real os spawning behind cap_guard(subprocess), run/spawn/stdio/wait/poll/pipeline/signals/groups, CXER4000-range mapping; all 27 are CXER0271 deny-lane cases (granted path verified manually); PTY returns CXER4009 where no portable openpty]']
    [module name=prof     gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete (25/25 ENFORCED, +1 skip): wall/cpu clocks (clock-cap-gated), counters, HDR histograms, trace, mem-snapshot, time-fn/time-and-trace thunks via prof_stdlib_builtin_env; per-program state reset']
    [module name=re       gate=enforced reason='RE2 impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green); 22 double-quote-convention expected-outputs re-derived via the real render_value (bare/single, SPEC-FINDINGS I)']
    [module name=store    gate=enforced reason='mem:// backend implemented (functional matrix + file:// deny paths)']
    [module name=test     gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete (ENFORCED, all cases green): assert-eq/true/false, assert-throws via [?fn] thunk through the eval.v env-hook, lifecycle hooks, assert-snapshot in-memory, assert-shape via validate-shape; test-009 fixture corrected to child-element record form (validate reads fields as children, validate.md §91 — SPEC-FINDINGS AD)']
    [module name=url      gate=enforced reason='RFC-3986 impl complete (ENFORCED, all cases green); url-032 fixture corrected — a map round-trip groups repeated key `a` per url.md §124 (key=insertion order), so a=1&a=3&b=2 is spec-faithful (SPEC-FINDINGS AD); 5 render-contract quote-convention expected-outputs re-derived via real render_value']
    [module name=validate gate=enforced reason='DATA-RECORD validator impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all 39 cases green, no carve-outs); failure outcome is the inspectable [invalid [violation…]] head not the propagating [err] sentinel (SPEC-FINDINGS AH; code.md §9.1.1); validate-with= custom field/record validators applied via the validate_stdlib_builtin_env eval-hook (invokes the user [?def], merges) and extends=$Base composition resolved via the value-reference + val_resolve_schema string-parse (SPEC-FINDINGS AH.1/AH.2 RESOLVED); 10 quote-convention expected-outputs re-derived via real render_value']
    [# SAP errors/effects/fp migration: fp IMPLEMENTED at Stage C Phase C4. #]
    [module name=fp gate=enforced reason='full §1 impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all 15 cases green): the six-combinator protocol map/flat-map/pure/traverse/sequence/fold dispatching on the head tag (sequence=Maybe+List, result=[ok]/[err]), E_NO_INSTANCE=cx-err:CXER4400 (D001) on an un-instanced tagged element; combinators are native fp-* prims (vcx/code/stdlib_fp.v) reached via the HOF env path since they apply a CX callable. Fixtures corrected: bracketed [$fn] callable args → bare $fn first-class refs (the established convention; [$fn] is a zero-arg call), and colon-bearing err code attrs quoted code=\'cx-err:CXER9999\' to parse (render emits bareword) — Stage-B authoring defects, D0xx C4']
    [# XAP module set — bus is the ordered-dispatch primitive (stdlib_bus.md §13.1). #]
    [module name=bus gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all 37 cases green): in-process pub/sub with synchronous, deterministic, ordered dispatch (descending priority, ties by registration order, §4.1) + re-entrant FIFO emission queue drained before the next external message (§4.2) + bounded cascade (max-cascade-depth/events → CXER4663, §4.4) + on-fault :isolate/:collect/:halt (§4.3); bus/close/on/off + introspection subscribers/topics/match/topic/matches; emit returns a [dispatch …] VALUE (zero subscribers → delivered=0, not a fault/absence, §2.3); [bus]/[subscription] closeable via [?with-open]. bus introduces NO capability (§5). One spec↔impl adaptation: the §2.2 prefix-glob :order.* uses ./* which the atom grammar (grammar.ebnf [6a]) forbids, so the SAME prefix-glob is spelled with - as the separator + a trailing - marker (:order- matches :order-placed); the CXPath-predicate pattern form is realized as a pure arity-1 boolean callable. CXER4661 (handle-race) is unreachable single-threaded.']
    [module name=journal gate=enforced reason='full §3 impl complete + spec-faithful: append-only hash-chained tenant-partitioned event log + deterministic fold→state, built ON store (persistence) + hash (chain links) + crypto.ed25519 (snapshot signing); no new capability (gated by store). open/attach/close, append (single mutating verb, optimistic expect-prev-seq → CXER4604), read/slice/since/query/head (out-of-range = absence (), not null/err), fold/fold-slice/fold-value/replay/dry-run (pure $fn enforced via the journal_stdlib_builtin_env eval-hook + node_calls_impure_builtin → CXER4611), verify/verify-slice (a present [verification valid=…] FINDING, not [err] — SAP §1; hash-mismatch/link-broken/seq-gap/genesis-invalid reasons), snapshot (signed [snapshot] over fold+anchor)/snapshot-verify/fold-from (fold ≡ full fold)/retain (prune-behind-signed-snapshot → CXER4616)/compact (copy-forward, source intact). Hermetic mem:// fixtures with a controllable clock so ts/hash are byte-stable']
    [module name=session gate=enforced reason='full §3 (principal,tenant) session impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green): the thin XAP session layer COMPOSES the shipped cx-stdlib/crypto jwt-verify (token verification delegated ENTIRELY, §2.2/N-SESSION-1) + cx-stdlib/http (Authorization/Cookie header reads + Set-Cookie writes) — session adds NO crypto and NO transport. FAIL-CLOSED attach (verify→map→bind→mirror-attach all-or-nothing); the four-channel split honored (unattached of→absence () NOT null NOT err; rejected attach→[err]; established→[session] value). Server-held registry (mirror-attach, by-id/by-client/of/from-cookie); opaque session id + CSRF synchronizer token are CSPRNG (never asserted by literal value — fixtures pin prefix/length/round-trip). CAPABILITY-FREE (no new cap, no effect_alignment entry — only net reach is crypto JWKS fetch). Error band CXER4800-4849: 4801 token-reject (wraps verbatim crypto fault as [cause]), 4802 no-tenant, 4803 no-principal, 4804 invalid/detached-op, 4805 rebind-refused (immutable binding), 4806 insecure-transport, 4807 no-token, 4808/4809 csrf-missing/mismatch, 4810/4811 cookie-insecure/unsafe-flags. Hermetic: reuses the crypto-071 golden RS256 token + literal JWKS + pinned now=[$time:datetime 2023 11 14 22 13 20]; tenant derived from the aud claim (no tid in the golden token).']
    [module name=authz gate=enforced reason='full §3 decision-layer impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all cases green): the single PEP decision function check/authorize over principals + attenuating/time-bounded/revocable delegations + guardian grants behind an incapacity-typed [gate …], plus the signed+versioned 6-predicate incapacity library, verify-tier (T0/T1/T2 M-of-N), effective envelope (intersection, most-restrictive-wins, unrecorded relationship ignored), dry-run/explain/trace. COMPOSES crypto/session/journal/store — adds NO crypto, NO transport, NO new caps-capability (capability-free in-memory store, no effect_alignment entry, mirroring session/journal). FOUR-CHANNEL: a decision is a present [permit]/[deny] VALUE (deny carries CXER4700 as DATA, NOT an [err]); check is TOTAL; an absent (revoked/expired/never-issued) grant is the absence channel () NOT null NOT [deny]; null is never produced. FAIL-CLOSED deny-by-default; guardian permits ONLY while its incapacity gate holds + ONLY its pinned [action …], flipping to [deny] the instant the principal re-engages (falsifiable-by-presence, no explicit revoke). BRIGHT LINE as a type constraint at AUTHORING: refusal-trigger leaf → CXER4701, state-only gate (<1 incapacity) → CXER4702, inline/ad-hoc predicate → CXER4706, escalation → CXER4703, T0-guardian/bad-sig/quorum-unmet → CXER4704, guardian↔ordinary shape mismatch + cross-tenant delegate + missing tenant → CXER4711, closed store → CXER4712. ONE grammar adaptation: the spec verb gate-wellformed? is spelled gate-wellformed (no trailing ?) — ? is not a NameChar in a call head [$authz:VERB …], the same constraint that forced net addr->string→addr-to-string (semantics identical, returns a [valid]/[invalid] VALUE not an [err]). Hermetic in-memory store + deterministic clock via as-of/until Unix-int + recorded signature markers (non-empty/non-invalid verifies T1; M-of-N quorum for T2) so negatives are testable without minting keys.']
    [module name=sched gate=enforced reason='full §3 durable-scheduler impl complete + spec-faithful (ENFORCED, all 36 cases green): after/at/every(fixed-delay|fixed-rate)/recur(a time [recurrence …] rule)/cron/cancel/timer-state + restore + test-clock-advance/clock-mode. sched is a THIN module that COMPOSES three shipped modules and adds NO calendar grammar, NO persistence, and NO new capability (§0/§5): time (next-occurrence re-arm + parse-cron + ::duration/::datetime), journal (durable [sched-intent …] append + restore fold), the picoev loop. Firing is $ev-shape-dispatched (§2.1): a zero-arg callable is invoked on the loop (return ignored), a [?channel] gets a [tick timer=<name>] posted. The DETERMINISTIC surface is enforced under the :manual virtual clock (virtual-now starts at the epoch; test-clock-advance drains due timers in deadline order, sleep-free, §4.2); the LIVE picoev held-open firing loop + the :wall production clock are the synthetic-transport part — gate=pending for a runtime-driven harness (so CXER4970 test-clock-under-:wall is UNREACHABLE from the public surface here, pinned by §7 footnote 1 only). on-missed (§2.5/§4.6): a single advance crossing N occurrences fires once under :skip/:coalesce, once-per-occurrence under :fire-all (recur COUNT-3 observed via :fire-all). [timer] is closeable via [?with-open] (close ≡ cancel, idempotent, never CXER0108) — the arming verbs are env-aware to stamp the close-id. Durable worker-recycle correctness: a named timer appends its intent to a journal; restore folds the journal to re-arm pending timers, binding $ev by name from the registry, surfacing an unbound name as an orphaned FINDING in the [restore-report …] (never silently dropped, §3.2). Error band CXER4970-4989: 4971 arg-invalid, 4972 mode/on-missed-invalid, 4973 durable-no-name, 4974 durable-no-journal, 4975 restore-intent-corrupt; a malformed cron surfaces time\'s CXER33xx unchanged (not a sched code); a raw effect in a fired callback without a grant hits CXER0271 at the callback effect point. Hermetic: :manual clock + mem:// journal so ts/hash/fires are byte-stable.']]]
